# **AVD — Release Notes (v1.0)**

## **Adaptive Visual Dynamics (AVD) — Official Public Release**

AVD reaches its first public version as an **emerging technical standard** designed to transform correctable optometric parameters into **adaptive visual rules** applicable to any digital interface.  
This release marks the complete publication of bilingual documentation and the consolidation of the algorithm as an open specification.

---

## **📘 Documentation included in this version**

- **README** — Main documentation in English  
- **README_es** — Spanish version of the README  
- **Technical Sheet** — Complete description of the standard  
- **AVD Algorithm** — Detailed algorithmic procedure  
- **Jurisdiction** — Informative note on legal interpretation  
- **MIT License** — Official English version + informative translation  

All documentation is available in **English and Spanish**, ensuring international accessibility and clarity.

---

## **🔧 Main features of version 1.0**

- Complete definition of the **AVD algorithmic procedure**  
- Normalization of optometric parameters: Sphere, Cylinder, Axis, Addition  
- Generation of adaptive visual rules:  
  - text size  
  - minimum contrast  
  - line and paragraph spacing  
  - optimal visual density  
- Construction of the **AVD visual profile**  
- Bilingual technical documentation  
- Repository structure prepared for future extensions  
- Official MIT License included

